Progressive wave in a periodic domain of one wavelength
=======================================================

A stream function wave (H = 0.125 m, T = 2 s, depth 0.4 m, wavelength 3.787 m),
the initial condition of every run, propagated for 15 periods (30 s) in a periodic
domain of one wavelength on four meshes (nx x nz = 95x20, 190x40, 380x80,
760x160). Case 0036 of each Part I study runs streamFunFoam, which evaluates the
exact solution, as the reference. Part I Section 6 and Appendix A; Part II
Sections 1, 3, 6 and 7.

Allrun runs the Part I studies, AllrunPartII the Part II studies.

Studies
-------

Part I (parmScanner, parameter file <study>.csv):
  solvers_maxCo             interFoam, interIsoFoam, interIsoGoam (geometric) under a
                            Courant limit, maxCo 0.5, 0.2, 0.1, 0.05 on each mesh
  solvers_fixedDt           the same with fixed time steps dt0, dt0/2, dt0/4, dt0/8,
                            dt0 = 0.02 s on 95x20, halved with each mesh refinement
  nLayers_maxCo             interIsoGoam with nLayers 1 and 2; every other study uses the
                            default, 2
  solvers_*_ddtCorrOff      the solver studies with PIMPLE ddtCorr no (Appendix A;
                            stock solvers as interFoamDdtCorr, interIsoFoamDdtCorr;
                            run/common/runDdtCorrOffStudy.sh)
Part II:
  finalSolver_maxCo,        fluxinator with laxWendroff + interfaceUpwind and its
  finalSolver_fixedDt       default explicit convection and ddtCorr off, on
                            the interIsoGoam cases of solvers_* (same case numbers;
                            finalSolver_buildMatrix.sh, finalSolver_runMatrix.py,
                            finalSolver_checkMatrix.py)
  finalSolverNoLW           the same without the Lax-Wendroff correction, cases 0014,
                            0017, 0020, 0026, 0029, 0032 and a fixed dt 0.02 s run
                            (runAll.sh)
  convection/<variant>_<mesh>_dt<dt>
                            the convection variants of Part II Section 6 at fixed dt,
                            from the Part I interIsoGoam case: implicit, crankNicolson,
                            explicit, explicitLW, explicitIU, explicitLWIU (the final
                            solver); the implicit, crankNicolson, explicit and
                            explicitLW runs carry budget_* fields of the former
                            PIMPLE switch momentumBudget (no longer used)
  momentumFlux/<case>       the four 190x40 convection cases of Part II Figure
                            fig:momFlux (implicit dt 0.005 and 0.0025, Crank-Nicolson
                            and explicit dt 0.005), rerun with the function object
                            convectiveMomentumFlux (system/controlDict)
  timing_maxCo0.1_noGauge/  time per step at max Co 0.1 without the wave gauge (Part II
                            Figure fig:selCost; data/timing_maxCo0.1.csv); see its README

Scripts
-------

analyseScan.py            accuracy and efficiency metrics per run (CSV in data/): wave
                          height error from a quadratic trend through all waves,
                          wave-to-wave scatter, shape and phase errors, spurious
                          velocities, cost
writeData.py              data/statistics.txt: derived numbers quoted in Part I
plotCrestHeight.py        crest, trough and wave height against time; shared functions

The paper figures and tables are made in papers/part1 and papers/part2 (one directory
per figure or table, named after its LaTeX label).

Requirements
------------

Stream function wave solution (streamFunFoam):
https://github.com/isoAdvector/streamFunctionWave

Wave gauge (function object surfacePosition, entry surfacePosition1 of the cases):
https://github.com/isoAdvector/surfacePosition

Running studies with parmScanner:
https://github.com/isoAdvector/cfdTools

Setting case entries (also used by parmScanner): dictator
https://github.com/isoAdvector/dictator

Post-processing: python3 with numpy, scipy and matplotlib.

Logs of some Part II runs name the solver interIsoGoamExt, now interIsoGoam.
